      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__sl__bt__resource_1gac43c1de372fd21b3cdacd15fca685caa" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>sl_status_t</type>
        <definition>sl_status_t sl_bt_resource_set_report_threshold</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint32_t low, uint32_t high)</argsstring>
        <name>sl_bt_resource_set_report_threshold</name>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>low</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>high</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Set low and high thresholds of memory buffer usage reports. Value 0 in parameter <computeroutput>low</computeroutput> for the low threshold disables the reporting, and a non-zero value in <computeroutput>low</computeroutput> enables the reporting.</para>
<para>When the reporting is enabled, event <ref refid="group__sl__bt__evt__resource__status" kindref="compound">sl_bt_evt_resource_status</ref> will be generated to report the status when the free buffer amount decreases and crosses the low threshold, and later another event will be generated if the free buffer amount increases and crosses the high threshold. If only the high threshold is crossed but the low threshold isn&apos;t, no event will be generated.</para>
<para>By default, low and high threshold values are 0, i.e., no report event is generated.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">low</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The low threshold of free bytes in the memory buffer, or 0 to disable the reporting </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">high</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A non-zero value as the high threshold that must be greater than parameter <computeroutput>low</computeroutput>, or 0 for not reporting the status for high threshold</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>SL_STATUS_OK if successful. Error code otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
