    <briefdescription>
<para>Resource Report. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Commands and events in this class can be used to query and receive the memory buffer usage status. The memory buffer is used by the Bluetooth stack for storing application data (e.g., API commands and events), user data over Bluetooth connections, advertising, scanning, etc. Total buffer size is defined by the application using the SL_BT_CONFIG_BUFFER_SIZE configuration. The Bluetooth stack does not partition the buffer, instead, the buffer is a shared resource for all features. Therefore, the available memory for one feature could be affected by another feature in simultaneous use cases. This API class provides a utility for application to get some insight of the buffer usage. As allocations in the memory buffer have overhead, the actual amount of memory that can be used for user data is less than a reported free memory amount. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
